---
description: Data-access conventions for repositories and data modules
globs: apps/api/{data,repositories}/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Data Access Layer

- Centralize all persistence reads/writes in data or repository modules.
- Expose storage through typed repository/store APIs instead of leaking storage internals.
- Keep methods focused on CRUD, mapping, and indexing operations.

# Layer Boundaries

- Do not implement business policy, workflow orchestration, or cross-domain decisions.
- Do not import HTTP framework types or construct API response payloads.
- Keep branching logic limited to persistence concerns (existence checks, mapping, indexing).

# Error Handling

- Normalize storage failures into consistent typed data-access errors.
- Include operation context in errors (operation name, entity type, identifier when available).
- Do not swallow I/O errors; throw or return explicit typed failures.

# Storage Abstraction

- Treat JSON/file storage as an implementation detail behind repository/store contracts.
- Keep direct file-system access inside dedicated storage utilities in this layer only.
- Keep service-facing method signatures storage-agnostic so backend storage can be replaced later.
